bnp-sidecar
===========

An unofficial, read-only command-line client for BNP Paribas account
information. It offers two independent backends:

- the Enable Banking PSD2 account-information API;
- a direct session against the BNP Paribas web application.

This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by BNP Paribas,
Enable Banking Oy, or any of their affiliates. Use it with your own account, at
your own risk, and in accordance with the terms of service of your bank and of
Enable Banking.

"BNP Paribas" and "Enable Banking" are trademarks of their respective owners.

The project does not implement payment initiation, transfers, orders or any
other write operation. It only reads account details, balances and
transactions.

- In Enable Banking mode, the account holder authorises access explicitly
  through the bank's own strong customer authentication flow in a browser.
- In direct mode, the account holder types their customer ID and 6-digit code
  in the terminal for each run, completes the bank's 2FA, and the sidecar sends
  only the read-only requests that the BNP web application performs. The code
  is never persisted, and session cookies stay in memory.

Enable Banking API documentation: https://enablebanking.com/docs/api/reference/
